    "open_questions": [
      "None Shall Escape the Judgement: transcribe it from the record (or a drum stem). The only tab is machine-made and mostly wrong; whether the snare is on 2 and 4 under the flying cymbal is not settled.",
      "Africa Unite (Survival, 1979): Survival credits him with it, but there is no tab of any kind; transcribe it.",
      "Every Peter Tosh song here but Bush Doctor follows a machine-made tab. Human transcriptions, or a check against drum stems, would let them be verified.",
      "Which tracks of Legalize It, Uprising and Mama Africa are his: the credits do not divide them. He names Ketchy Shuby, Coming In From the Cold and Mama Africa.",
      "The flying cymbal with the Aggrovators beyond this one record (Joshua's Word, Move Out of Babylon, Cornell Campbell): who drummed on which.",
      "His kits by year: a big kit of red shells with chrome rims at the Greek in 1983 (the film); no make found."
    ]
  },
