    "roles": ["session", "band_member", "touring"],
    "summary": "The Soul Syndicate's drummer from 1969 and Bunny Lee's in the Aggrovators: on Johnny Clarke's None Shall Escape the Judgement (1974) he played the hi-hat opened on every off-beat, after MFSB's Philadelphia records, and Bunny Lee named it the flying cymbal and put it on everything. He did not invent it, he says. Over two hundred records in the 1970s, Africa Unite and Coming In From the Cold for Bob Marley, Ketchy Shuby on Legalize It; then Peter Tosh's drummer from 1981, through Mama Africa and No Nuclear War, until Tosh was murdered in 1987, a shooting Davis survived. Later Big Mountain, and Ziggy Marley's drummer today. 'A wild kind of drummer ... really aggressive' by his own account."
  },
